Key insight: **crap4js reports CC=11 for findMatchingBrace at 100% coverage → CRAP=11**. My hand count was wrong — Istanbul/crap4js counts each `||`/`&&` in the conditions: line 469 `c === "'" || c === '"' || c === '` = 2 logical ops, line 465/466 each 1, line 462 loop 1, line 464 if 1, 470 if 1, 471 if 1, 473 if 1 → CC = 1 + 1(for) + 1 + 1 + 1 + 2 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 11. Yes — 11.

All my other fixes landed well (_envBridge 7.8, everything else ≤ 7). Only findMatchingBrace exceeds: must get CC ≤ 8. Options:

1. Simplify the quote-char test: `if (c === "'" || c === '"' || c === '`')` — 2 ||s. Replace with indexOf: `if ('\\"\'`'.indexOf(c) !== -1)` — hmm messy. Or a helper `isQuoteChar(c)` — but then the loop still has CC: for(1) + if-quote(1) + if-escape(1) + if-endquote(1) + if-open(1) + if-close(1) + if-depth0(1) = 8. Plus function base 1 → 8! `isQuoteChar` itself CC 3 (2 ||s). Main loop: 1 + 1(for) + 1(464) + 1(465) + 1(466) + 1(470) + 1(471) + 1(473) = 8 → CRAP 8 at 100% = 8.0, not > 8 ✓ (threshold fails only >8). But 100% coverage must hold (it does now).

2. Reduce branches: restructure using a small state machine? Overkill.

Go with isQuoteChar helper:

```js
function isQuoteChar(c) {
   return c === "'" || c === '"' || c === '`';
}

function findMatchingBrace(src, start) {
   var depth = 0;
   var quote = null;
   for (var i = start; i < src.length; i++) {
       var c = src[i];
       if (quote) {
           if (c === '\\') { i++; continue; }
           if (c === quote) quote = null;
           continue;
       }
       if (isQuoteChar(c)) { quote = c; continue; }
       if (c === '{') { depth++; continue; }
       if (c === '}') {
           depth--;
           if (depth === 0) return i;
       }
   }
   return -1;
}
```

findMatchingBrace CC: base 1 + for 1 + if(quote) 1 + if(\\) 1 + if(quote-end) 1 + if isQuote 1 + if { 1 + if } 1 + if depth0 1 = 9. Hmm still 9? Istanbul CC counts each if + for + &&/||. Let me count decision points: for(1), if-quote(1), if-backslash(1), if-c===quote(1), if-isQuote(1), if-open(1), if-close(1), if-depth0(1) = 8 + 1 base = 9. Still 9 > 8.

Need CC ≤ 8. Remove one more decision: merge the escape handling? Combine open-brace handling into the close check:

```js
if (c === '{') { depth++; continue; }
if (c === '}') { depth--; if (depth === 0) return i; }
```
Alternative: handle depth via else-if chain reducing... decisions count same.

Restructure — handle quoted state first, then a switch-like depth update:

```js
for (var i = start; i < src.length; i++) {
   var c = src[i];
   if (quote) {
       if (c === '\\') { i++; continue; }
       if (c === quote) quote = null;
       continue;
   }
   if (isQuoteChar(c)) { quote = c; continue; }
   if (c === '{') depth++;
   else if (c === '}') {
       depth--;
       if (depth === 0) return i;
   }
```
if-open(1) + else-if-close(1) — istanbul counts else-if as one decision? istanbul counts if paths: `if (a) ... else if (b)` = 2 branch points but CC +2 (each if adds 1). Same.

Hmm. Reduce inside-quote handling: `if (c === '\\') {i++; continue;} if (c === quote) quote = null; continue;` — could become:
```js
if (quote) {
   if (c === '\\') i++;
   else if (c === quote) quote = null;
   continue;
}
```
Wait the original `if (c=='\\') { i++; continue; }` skips the next char. With else-if: if backslash → i++ and then continue anyway → the escaped char is skipped by loop increment (i++ in loop + i++ here = skips one). Original: i++ then continue then loop i++ → also skips one. Equivalent! And consolidates: decisions: if(quote) 1, if(\\) 1, else-if(quote) 1, continue (0). Same count as before (the two ifs were already 2). No gain.

Count again what istanbul gives: base 1; for +1; if(quote) +1; if(\\) +1; if(c===quote) +1; if(isQuoteChar) +1; if({) +1; if(}) +1; if(depth===0) +1 → 9.

Cut the `if (depth === 0) return i;` by returning on depth check differently? It's needed.

Cut `for` by using indexOf scanning? Alternative algorithm: use a regex to strip strings before counting? E.g.:

```js
function findMatchingBrace(src, start) {
   var depth = 0;
   var body = src.substring(start);
   // mask string literals so their braces don't count
   var masked = body.replace(/'(?:[^'\\]|\\.)*'|"(?:[^"\\]|\\.)*"|`(?:[^`\\]|\\.)*`/g, function(m) {
       return m.replace(/./g, '); // hmm replaces with spaces, same length? not exactly with newlines
   });
   ...
}
```
Regex-based masking is fragile (multiline strings, etc.).

Different approach — reduce decisions by combining quote-open detection with the quote variable:

```js
for (var i = start; i < src.length; i++) {
   var c = src[i];
   if (quote) {
       if (c === '\\') { i++; continue; }
       if (c === quote) quote = null;
       continue;
   }
   if (isQuoteChar(c)) { quote = c; continue; }
   if (c !== '{' && c !== '}') continue;  // 2 decisions
   depth += c === '{' ? 1 : -1;           // 1
   if (depth === 0) return i;             // 1
}
```
for(1) if-quote(1) if-\\(1) if-c===quote(1) if-isQuote(1) if-c!=={ && c!==}(2!) ternary(1) if-depth0(1) = base1+9 = 10. Worse.

OK the real hog: 8 decision points inside. Extract the QUOTED-state handling into its own function returning new index:

```js
// Index just past the quoted run starting at `i` (the opening quote is
// src[i]); handles escaped characters. Returns the index of the closing
// quote, or src.length - 1 when unterminated.
function skipQuoted(src, i) {
   var quote = src[i];
   for (i = i + 1; i < src.length; i++) {
       if (src[i] === '\\') { i++; continue; }
       if (src[i] === quote) return i;
   }
   return src.length - 1;
}

function findMatchingBrace(src, start) {
   var depth = 0;
   for (var i = start; i < src.length; i++) {
       var c = src[i];
       if (isQuoteChar(c)) { i = skipQuoted(src, i); continue; }
       if (c === '{') { depth++; continue; }
       if (c === '}') {
           depth--;
           if (depth === 0) return i;
       }
   }
   return -1;
}
```
skipQuoted CC: 1 + for 1 + if(\\) 1 + if(quote) 1 = 4. findMatchingBrace CC: 1 + for 1 + if-isQuote 1 + if-{ 1 + if-} 1 + if-depth0 1 = 6. isQuoteChar: 1 + 2 = 3. All ≤ 8. At 100% coverage CRAP = CC ✓. Need test coverage for skipQuoted paths: existing messy test (escape + quote-end), normal strings everywhere, unterminated quote case — my 'broken' test has unterminated BODY but not unterminated STRING. Add a fixture with an unterminated string inside a body: `function x() { var s = 'never closed; }` — then skipQuoted runs to end, returns len-1, continue, loop ends, findMatchingBrace returns -1 → body null. Add that to the broken test or a new one.

Wait, subtle semantics difference: original counted braces INSIDE nothing; strings skipped entirely — same. Escaped backslash before quote: `'it\\'s'` — skipQuoted: at `\\` → i++ skips the backslash... wait `src[i] === '\\'` — the string in source is `\'` (backslash, quote). skipQuoted sees `\` → i++ skips `'`, continue → `s` not quote... until closing `'` → return. ✓.

Template literals with ${...} containing braces — masked as string; original had same behavior (quote = '`' until next backtick). Same.

Update implementation + add unterminated-string test.

